[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343543326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111002#issuecomment-3343543326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111002","id":3343543326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7HSmwe","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-28T14:23:41Z","updated_at":"2025-09-28T14:24:26Z","body":"Moving to the main Godot repository, as this issue is not specific to godot-cpp.\n\n> We should call MessgeQueue:: flush\n\nAre you sure it's safe to flush the message queue after the process has crashed? There's little we can assume to be working once the engine is in a \"crashed\" state.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343543326/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343630550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111002#issuecomment-3343630550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111002","id":3343630550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7HS8DW","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-28T14:50:31Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T11:49:28Z","body":"Hm. So, like @Calinou mentions above, I don't think we can _guaranty_ that a message would be shown, because we don't know why we are crashing, and it could be something severe.\n\nBut `CRASH_COND_MSG()` should have fully sent the error message from the GDExtension to the Godot side before it quits. If godot-cpp had a way to also try and force Godot to flush messages, that could make it more likely that the error message would travel through the debugger from Godot to the editor.\n\nWe don't appear to have a way to do that - it's probably something we'd need to add to `gdextension_interface.h`? We'd also need to make sure that it wouldn't be abused.\n\nAlso, looking at the version of `CRASH_COND_MSG()` within Godot itself, it looks like it _also_ doesn't flush the message queue, and so would also be just as likely to not get its message back to the editor. So, it doesn't seem like GDExtension is worse than a Godot module in this regard.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343630550/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3345019264","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111002#issuecomment-3345019264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111002","id":3345019264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7HYPGA","user":{"login":"MYTNB","id":31533351,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTMzMzUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31533351?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB","html_url":"https://github.com/MYTNB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-29T05:30:57Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T05:32:40Z","body":"> Moving to the main Godot repository, as this issue is not specific to godot-cpp.\n> \n> > We should call MessgeQueue:: flush\n> \n> Are you sure it's safe to flush the message queue after the process has crashed? There's little we can assume to be working once the engine is in a \"crashed\" state.\n\nBecause I want to see in the editor where the process crashes (at least when running through the editor). Sometimes I have to add assertions like assert, but I can't get the crashing stack information on the editor, so I have to repeatedly modify my plugin to locate it\n\nPerhaps adding a new CRASH-MSG to GODOT-CPP would be better? It will immediately send a crash message to the editor","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3345019264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]